3.2.2. Actor-Critic Methods
The one-step advantage actor-critic (A2C) is analogous to the TD methods introduced above, which do not involve offline policy improvement steps. A2C implements the notion of δt, the difference between the expected value and actual value for a given state and state-value weighting w [15].
δt = Rt+1 + γvˆ(st+1, w) − vˆ(st, w) (17)
